menu "Gateway: firmware updates (FW-1)"

    config GW_FW_SELFCHECK_S
        int "Least uptime of a new firmware before its self-check confirms it (s)"
        range 10 600
        default 60
        help
            Issue #144: a new image boots on trial. The self-check confirms it at the first
            instant when the uptime is at least this value, the gateway is in its expected
            mode, the network driver started and the web server loop is alive. It does not
            depend on the broker, the Modbus slaves, NTP or the update server. A reset
            before the confirmation (crash, watchdog, power cut) returns to the earlier
            image.

    config GW_FW_BACKSTOP_S
        int "Uptime at which a new firmware whose self-check is not true is rejected (s)"
        range 60 3600
        default 300
        help
            Issue #144: without a true self-check at this uptime, the image is rejected
            (planned restart: the bootloader returns to the earlier image). An esp_timer does
            the same 10 s later when the main task is blocked.

    config GW_FW_BOOTLOOP_CLEAR_S
        int "Uptime in normal mode that clears the boot-loop counter (s)"
        range 10 3600
        default 120
        help
            Issue #144: the boot-loop counter (crash resets in a row, RTC memory) starts safe
            mode at 3. It is cleared after this uptime in normal mode.

    config GW_FW_SAFE_MODE_MIN
        int "Duration of safe mode before normal mode is tried again (min)"
        range 1 1440
        default 60
        help
            Issue #144: safe mode (recovery mode with the cause "repeated crashes") ends
            after this time with a restart, and the counter at 2: one more crash starts safe
            mode again. A restart by the operator or a power cycle also ends it.

    config GW_FW_HTTP_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "Network timeout of a firmware download (ms)"
        range 1000 60000
        default 10000

    config GW_FW_TASK_STACK
        int "Stack of the download task (bytes)"
        range 6144 16384
        default 8192
        help
            The task exists only while a download runs (TLS handshake included), or while
            the image of the other slot is verified (the "Restart into" button).

    config GW_FW_TASK_PRIORITY
        int "Priority of the download task"
        range 1 7
        default 2

    config GW_FW_PARK_OTHER_CORE
        bool "Park the other core while an image is verified (QEMU only)"
        depends on GW_IO_SIMULATED
        default n
        help
            Espressif's QEMU does not model the ESP32-S3 cache freeze that flash mappings
            use: code the other core runs from flash during esp_image_verify() makes QEMU
            abort. With this option a high-priority task spins in IRAM on the other core
            for those calls. Not needed (and not wanted) on the chip: there it would stop
            core 1, where the RS485 bus owner runs, during a real update. So it is only
            offered in the emulator build (GW_IO_SIMULATED).

endmenu
